+## Self-host acceptance gate
+
+The standalone private test-driver route
+`python3 tools/test_policy.py tool self-host-acceptance` is an availability
+gate, not a new public `chibi` command. It currently prints `UNSUPPORTED` and
+returns 2 before test initialization. No compiler runs, no fixture passes, and
+no stage-one or stage-two artifact is produced. This deliberate nonzero result
+must remain visible; do not convert it to a successful expected-failure check,
+or replace it with success when a component differential passes.
+[Resource admission](testing.md#self-host-acceptance-availability) is separate.
+
+### Missing executable contracts
+
+The current product interfaces cannot perform the complete acceptance sequence:
+
+- `compiler_fixture_prepare_packs` calls the native
+  `authoring_packages_prepare`, which owns `script_analyze_package`,
+  `script_lower_package` and module finalization. The existing
+  `compiler-artifact` case uses that path to prepare eight packages, then
+  serializes the source-snapshot closure. Its exported `Build` entry returns
+  package snapshot results. It does not compile its own implementation.
+- `chibi-compiler-host` accepts an already prepared artifact, entry ID and JSON
+  arguments. Its runtime-only link closure excludes native source analysis and
+  lowering. Text, arrays, JSON and raw syntax capabilities do not supply a
+  complete authored compiler entry or authored executable-artifact construction.
+  The host transports execution; it is not itself a Chibi-authored compiler.
+- `chibi build PROJECT` still invokes the native project compiler. The installed
+  `Build.chibi` still invokes CMake and three Python helpers. Neither is an
+  installed Chibi-owned compiler/build/link replacement.
+
+The missing implementation is a complete authored compiler program and its
+explicit source-input, diagnostic and artifact-output contract over the existing
+package/runtime boundaries. Its reviewed entry identity and complete dependency
+closure must be known before a harness can invoke it. This document does not
+invent a `Compile` export, source manifest format, shipping command or new syntax.
+Component, transport, retained-reader and scalar-lowering increments retain their
+own tests; do not duplicate them in this availability gate.
+
+### Required replacement of the unsupported gate
+
+Once the complete compiler exists, replace the early refusal with C/pico_unit
+cases in the existing `test_tools` dispatcher. Independently review the actual
+entry/output contract and exact bounded workload before running it. The complete
+sequence must establish all of the following:
+
+1. Freeze the clean candidate and the entire compiler source closure, including
+   all imported compiler/core sources, generated inputs, binding identities and
+   target/format identities. Record paths and content hashes. A selected subset
+   of compiler components is not a complete source closure.
+2. Stage zero compiles that closure into the stage-one compiler artifact. Record
+   bootstrap compiler identity and minimum compatible version. A fresh
+   runtime-only process loads stage one; it cannot call native source analysis,
+   native lowering, another compiler process, or a stage-zero compile service.
+   Narrow raw-parser/backend/runtime ABIs remain declared dependencies.
+3. Stage one receives the same source bytes and target inputs and emits a fresh
+   stage-two compiler artifact through authored compiler policy. Record artifact
+   provenance and reject missing, stale, partial or copied outputs. Independently
+   load and exercise stage two in a fresh runtime-only process.
+4. Compile the same checked semantic, invalid-source diagnostic, ABI and artifact
+   fixtures using stages one and two. Compare acceptance, diagnostic category,
+   ranges/order, declarations/layouts, artifact-format identities and decoded
+   observable behavior. Execute resulting fixtures on BYTECODE and SLJIT with
+   actual backend-entry counters and no fallback. Reuse the existing fixtures
+   and production codecs. Do not substitute an oracle's compiled output. Require
+   byte equality only where determinism has separately been established.
+5. Exercise the normal installed workflow and repeat after relocation, with
+   original installation/source/build/cache paths inaccessible. Supply the
+   pinned compiler sources from a clean checkout and build/link a checked game
+   through the stable commands. Verify declared formats and bounded observable
+   game behavior. A prebuilt game's successful launch proves neither building
+   nor linking; a game cache hit is not a clean-build proof.
+6. Separate allowed bootstrap inputs from final required inputs. In the final
+   installed/relocated environment, make `cmake`, `clang` and `gcc` unavailable,
+   including renamed binaries, absolute paths, wrappers, remote compiler
+   services and populated caches that conceal those requirements. Emptying PATH
+   or installing fake successful commands is insufficient. Use a reviewed
+   minimal filesystem/process boundary with an explicit executable/library/input
+   allowlist and provenance. Record the actual final linker, assembler, backend,
+   platform SDK, runtime libraries and version/license identities; do not infer
+   that they are absent merely because the three tool names were absent.
+
+Stage-zero setup may still use CMake, native C/C++ compilers, Python helpers and
+native build tools. A library API such as SLJIT or a future LLVM binding is
+distinct from invoking a compiler executable. Final dependency claims follow
+the actual link/load closure and process provenance; this gate does not decide
+which currently permitted native dependencies the completed implementation needs.
+
+The runtime acceptance sequence remains subject to one shared production
+60-second ceiling. Stage-zero configuration and test-driver compilation are
+separate, but the stage-chain and game operations under test cannot be hidden
+there as setup. If the complete sequence cannot fit a reviewed admitted
+workload, it stays blocked; do not split it into passing chunks, extend the
+deadline, omit sources or substitute prepared outputs. Windows process support
+and supported-host coverage remain separate unfinished requirements. No
+stage-zero recovery path or native implementation is deleted by this increment.
+
