+## Self-host acceptance availability
+
+`tool self-host-acceptance` selects a fixed unsupported branch in the existing
+native `test_tools` dispatcher. It writes one fixed diagnostic (less than 512
+bytes) and exits 2 before `tool_init`, pico_unit initialization or product calls.
+It has zero test cases, assertions, compiler preparations, authored calls, module
+finalizations, workload children, frames, GPU or network work. Its only workload
+I/O is the diagnostic on stderr. The production supervisor launches the driver
+and owns the shared
+60-second deadline and process cleanup.
+
+This standalone route is outside all aggregates. Registration records neither
+first-run admission nor a measured result. Independent exact-source/resource
+review is required before its first supervised invocation, with driver
+configuration/build timing separate. Its expected nonzero result is
+`UNSUPPORTED`, never a self-hosting pass or measured compiler coverage. Do not
+wrap the selector in failure suppression to obtain a green acceptance result.
+Static patch/syntax checks do not establish that the driver built or ran.
+
+Replace the refusal only after the
+[complete stage-chain and installed/relocated contract](self-hosting-build.md#self-host-acceptance-gate)
+has real product entrypoints and a finite reviewed C/pico_unit workload.
+Component parity, process orchestration and the existing `compiler-artifact`
+roundtrip remain distinct evidence. They do not admit or complete that future
+workload.
